 "coord_accuracy": "site",
 "category": "Cultural",
 "category_zh": "文化遗产",
 "category_en": "Cultural",
 "criteria": "(iii)(vi)",
 "year": "2016",
 "danger": false,
 "transnational": true,
 "intro_zh": "该系列遗产由位于波斯尼亚和黑塞哥维那、塞尔维亚西部、黑山西部以及克罗地亚中部和南部的 28 个遗址组成，代表了这些墓地和具有地区特色的中世纪墓碑（或称 stećci）。这些墓地的历史可追溯至公元 12 世纪至 16 世纪，按照中世纪欧洲的常见习俗，按行排列。 stećci 大多由石灰石雕刻而成。它们具有广泛的装饰图案和铭文，代表了中世纪欧洲的图像连续性以及当地独特的传统。",
 "intro_zh_source": "machine_translation",
 "intro_en": "This serial property combines 28 sites, located in Bosnia and Herzegovina, western Serbia, western Montenegro and central and southern Croatia, representing these cemeteries and regionally distinctive medieval tombstones, or stećci. The cemeteries, which date from the 12th to 16th centuries CE, are laid out in rows, as was the common custom in Europe from the Middle Ages. The stećci are mostly carved from limestone. They feature a wide range of decorative motifs and inscriptions that represent iconographic continuities within medieval Europe as well as locally distinctive traditions.",
 "intro_en_source": "unesco_official",
 "intro_local": "Stećci, srednjovjekova groblja s nadgrobnim spomenicima je naziv za srednjovjekovna groblja sa stećcima koja su upisana na UNESCO-ov popis mjesta svjetske baštine u Europi na 40. zasjedanju odbora UNESCO-a u Istanbulu 15. srpnja 2016. godine. Dana 2. studenog 2009. godine, ministarstva kulture zemalja Bosne i Hercegovine, Hrvatske, Srbije i Crne Gore su zajednički nominirala stećke za upis na UNESCO-ov popis mjesta svjetske baštine, kao svoju zajedničku baštinu.",
 "intro_local_source": "wikipedia",
